  "interpretation": [
    "The constructor is given no internal human segmentor or FOV estimator; it prints unconditional capability warnings. Per-image external masks and cam_int are independent supported branches.",
    "External masks get score 1, share the RGB affine crop, and pass through the configured learned mask_downscaling -> body image embeddings path. MASK_EMBED_TYPE=v2 and MASK_PROMPT=v1 are enabled. The checkpoint auditor records 18 loaded learned mask prompt tensors and zero learned weight mismatches.",
    "No new SAM2 segmentation is executed in the consumer. The already received, reviewed SAM2 masks are consumed. RGB background is not simply zeroed by the mask.",
    "Full inference first runs the mask-conditioned body decoder. Its predicted hand boxes seed separate RGB hand passes. Those prepare_batch calls pass camera but no external masks and therefore have mask_score zero. MediaPipe is a later independent RGB observer.",
    "The explicit six-field original-pixel camera is converted to float32 without adding half a pixel. process_one_image overwrites its initially prepared default batch K before run_inference. Body and hand rays, camera translation and original camera-head projection use the supplied camera.",
    "Upstream full-mode final SAM70 projection overwrites its earlier K-correct projection using fx for both axes and width/2,height/2 for principal point. Thus its returned raw SAM70 2D seeds are not a byte-exact projection under the supplied six-field K. Native 3D output is not shifted by this last 2D overwrite.",
    "Our downstream native fitting/review copies raw camera_intrinsics.npy; review_human projects 3D vertices/joints with the full saved K. This does not validate metric scale, physical contact, hidden hands or official accuracy."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "This is source-trace plus saved-output consistency evidence, not an activation-hook capture of every model call or an ablation proving a quality benefit from masks.",
    "The camera is a MoGe2 estimate, not measured calibration. The upstream camera-translation parameterization uses fx, while rays and the initial perspective projector use full K.",
    "The upstream final raw 2D overwrite has an approximately +0.5 pixel offset per axis for the received centered cameras. Supplied fx/fy differ slightly; the y residual also contains that difference.",
    "Neither full coverage nor mask/camera consumption establishes successful physical grasp or challenge compliance."
  ],
